<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmen 1996 cotton crop slumps to 430,000 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Turkmen 1996 cotton crop slumps to 430,000 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan harvested only 430,000 tonnes of raw cotton in 1996, far below last year's 1.3 million, state television said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The harvest is a fraction of the 1996 target of 1.5 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The television report said the main reason for the poor harvest was the large backlog of unpaid salaries to cotton workers.</p>
<p>In September, agriculture ministry officials said the cotton crop had been hit by frost and pests.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
